<%= render layout: "pages/frame", locals: { title: t("pages.support_title") } do %>
  <p>Help with using <strong><%= @legal[:product_name] %></strong> on the website and on iPhone.</p>

  <h2>Contact us</h2>
  <%= render "pages/operator" %>

  <h2>Health data does not show up in Life</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Open the app and tap Health &gt; Sync now.</li>
    <li>Check the permissions in Settings &gt; Health &gt; Data Access &amp; Devices &gt; Life. Each data type must be turned on.</li>
    <li>To sync while the app is closed, keep Background App Refresh on and do not force-quit the app.</li>
    <li>While the iPhone is locked, the system does not release health data. The upload happens after you unlock it.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Screen time is behind</h2>
  <p>iPhone screen time reaches Life through a Mac, and only after the day is over. The previous day usually appears between late morning and early afternoon.</p>

  <h2>How to connect an AI assistant</h2>
  <p>On the website, open Setup &gt; AI assistants, copy the server address and add it as a connector in your assistant. It opens Life for you to sign in and authorize. Access is read-only unless you allow changes, and can be revoked on the same page.</p>

  <h2>How to delete my account</h2>
  <p>In the app, under Account &gt; Delete my account. On the website, at <%= link_to "#{request.base_url}/delete-account", delete_account_path %>. Deletion erases the user and all data, and cannot be undone.</p>

  <h2>Privacy</h2>
  <p>See the <%= link_to "Privacy Policy", privacy_path %> and the <%= link_to "Terms of Use", terms_path %>.</p>
<% end %>
